<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lanzhou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lanzhou is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a> province in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a>. Known in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui</a> times as Jincheng, it guarded a crossing of the Yellow River on the road to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu-corridor">Hexi Corridor</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a>, and was the base of the rebel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xue-ju">Xue Ju</a>, who founded a short-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> state in 617. It is today a major industrial and transport centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lanzhou.jpg" alt="Lanzhou" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Megalizard29 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_Lanzhou_August_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
